apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: triage-runbooks
  namespace: {{ triage_namespace }}
data:
  runbooks.yaml: |
    WorkloadPodCrashLooping: |
      1. Use Kubernetes MCP (get_workload_status or describe_pod) in the alert namespace to identify the restarting pod, exit code, and events (OOMKilled, BackOff, Unhealthy probe).
      2. Fetch previous container logs using get_pod_logs(previous=True) or search_logs in Elasticsearch for ERROR/WARN lines.
      3. Use Prometheus MCP (query_range) to check container memory vs limits if OOM is suspected.
    LogstashNotIngesting: |
      1. Check Logstash pod status and events in namespace logging via Kubernetes MCP.
      2. Check Prometheus up{job=~".*logstash.*"} and recent restarts.
      3. Inspect Logstash pod logs for pipeline, Grok, or Elasticsearch connection errors.
    FilebeatDown: |
      1. Check Filebeat DaemonSet pods and events in namespace logging via Kubernetes MCP.
      2. Inspect Filebeat pod logs for permission errors on /var/log/containers or connection refused to logstash:5044.
    ElasticsearchClusterUnhealthy: |
      1. Check elasticsearch-master StatefulSet pods and events in namespace logging via Kubernetes MCP.
      2. Check Prometheus for elasticsearch_cluster_health_status and node disk/memory pressure.
      3. Inspect Elasticsearch pod logs for unassigned shards or heap/GC errors.
    GCPExporterDown: |
      1. Check gcp-stackdriver-exporter pod and events in namespace monitoring via Kubernetes MCP.
      2. Check Prometheus up{job=~".*gcp.*|.*stackdriver.*"}.
      3. Inspect exporter pod logs for OAuth/Workload Identity or API quota errors.
